# The Stilo library

Functions for Stilo documents, written in Swan. `stilo init` copies this
folder into a project's `lib/stilo/`. This document binds one name,
`stilo`, a namespace of functions; a document of the project imports it
with `texl.import "~/lib/stilo/stilo.texl"` and binds `lib.data.stilo`
(the full tag is in `docs/texl-lib.md`; it cannot be quoted here, where
it would run).

*A placeholder for now: the first real function, `stilo.dataframe`, comes
with the data cell.*

- `stilo.greet name` — the text "Hello, name!".

<% stilo = {
    greet: name -> "Hello, " + name + "!"
} %>
